// "Mill N" ([CR#701.17a]): the imperative YOU-form self-mill — you put the top
// N cards of your library into your graveyard as one group; a single
// instruction, clamped to library size ([CR#701.17b]). A SLICE-family keyword
// action (like draw): a `Batch(N, ...)` over the per-unit `Composite` named
// "Mill" whose body describes the top slice of your library moving to your
// graveyard (a `MoveGroup` over `TopOfLibrary`, `whose` defaulting You). The
// `Batch` gives a count-doubling replacement (Bruvac, [CR#121.2a,616.1g]) ONE
// aggregate window to bite, and the engine commits the whole top slice as ONE
// simultaneous batch of per-card, individually-redirectable moves (Rest in
// Peace bites each, [CR#616.1]) — NOT the per-card SEQUENCE a draw is
// ([CR#121.2]). The declarative-subject form ("Target player mills N cards.")
// is the `Mills(who, n)` macro; this is the bare you-imperative.
//
// Usage: Mill(3) -> "Mill three cards."
(
    name: "Mill",
    template: "mill ${0:card|cards}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect, KeywordAction],
    params: [Count],
    body: Batch(Param(0), Composite(
        name: Mill,
        body: MoveGroup(
            group: TopOfLibrary(count: 1),
            arrangement: AnyOrder,
            to: Graveyard,
        ),
    )),
)
